#4. A handwriting recognition model adjusts its weights during training to reduce prediction errors. The current weight vector is W=[0.7,0.5,0.9], the gradient vector is G=[0.2,0.1,0.3], and the learning rate is 0.1. Write a Python program to update the weights using the gradient descent rule and display the updated weight vector.
import numpy as np

W = np.array([0.7, 0.5, 0.9])
G = np.array([0.2, 0.1, 0.3])
lr = 0.1

new_W = W - lr * G

print("Updated Weights:", new_W)
